@startuml training-embedding-pipeline
' Subword-embedding training as the code actually executes it: a vocabulary pass
' that lowercases and frequency-filters, matrix initialisation, construction of
' the unigram^(3/4) negative-sampling table, then one pass per epoch with a
' linearly decayed learning rate. The two entry points differ only in how the
' epoch passes get their sentences: `train` buffers the whole corpus in RAM,
' `train_streaming` re-reads the corpus once per epoch from a reader factory.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/training-embedding-pipeline.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/training/embedding.md §3.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #ECEFF1
  BorderColor #546E7A
  FontColor #263238
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title Embedding training — skip-gram with negative sampling

rectangle "**CorpusReader**" as reader #455A64

rectangle "**Pass 1 — vocabulary**\nlowercase · split_whitespace\nkeep count ≥ min_count\nsort by frequency desc" as vocab #2E7D32
rectangle "**Initialise**\nSubwordEmbedding(|V|, dim,\nbuckets = 2 000 000)\nsubword n-grams of length 3…6" as init #2E7D32
rectangle "**Negative sampler**\ntable of 10⁷ slots drawn ∝ c(w)^(3/4)" as sampler #2E7D32

rectangle "**Epoch e = 0 … E−1**\nlr_e = lr₀ · (1 − e/E)" as epoch #2E7D32
rectangle "**Per centre word**\nsub-sample frequent words\ndraw window ~ U{1..window_size}\nskip-gram update over the context\n+ k negative samples" as update #2E7D32

rectangle "**SubwordEmbedding**\nword vectors ⊕ subword buckets" as model #2E7D32
rectangle "**embed.bin**" as out #455A64

rectangle "**train(reader)**\nbuffers all sentences in RAM\n(warns above 10⁶ sentences)" as buffered #546E7A
rectangle "**train_streaming(factory)**\nre-reads the corpus each epoch\n(bounded memory)" as streaming #546E7A

reader --> vocab
vocab --> init
init --> sampler
sampler --> epoch

buffered --> epoch : sentences\nfrom RAM
streaming --> epoch : fresh reader\nper epoch

epoch --> update
update --> epoch : next centre word
epoch --> model : all epochs done
model --> out

note right of update
  OOV words are representable at query
  time because a word vector is the sum of
  its subword-bucket vectors — the FastText
  property that gives the hybrid its OOV arm.
end note

@enduml
